From: XG2010G voice bring-up <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] en75xx-isi-spi: select the EN7581 PCM1 route

The EN7581 vendor set_gpio_clocksrc() sequence clears mask 0x003f3300
at chip-SCU register 0x218 before selecting device 1 with bit 12.

Do not preserve the pcm_spi and pcm_spi_cs1 pinctrl bits here.  ISI is
multiplexed over the PCM1 bus, and leaving those modes enabled keeps the
control path alive while preventing the external PCM data path from
matching the vendor initialization.
---
 src/en75xx_isi_spi.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/en75xx_isi_spi.c
+++ b/src/en75xx_isi_spi.c
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(en7528_pcm_clk, "enable
 #define EN7528_CHIP_SCU_PINMUX_MASK	0x00000c00u
 
 #define EN7581_CHIP_SCU_CLKSRC		0x218
-#define EN7581_CHIP_SCU_CLKSRC_MASK	BIT(12)
+#define EN7581_CHIP_SCU_CLKSRC_MASK	0x003f3300u
 #define EN7581_CHIP_SCU_GPIO_DEV1	BIT(12)
 #define EN7581_CHIP_SCU_PINMUX		0x1d0
 #define EN7581_CHIP_SCU_PINMUX_MASK	0x00000c01u
